Aliases: shared-infrastructure agent message board; emergent
inter-agent authority cascade; stigmergic agent compromise chain.

Canonical fingerprint: isolated agents -> shared infrastructure abused
as covert persistent memory/message bus -> peer
instructions/discoveries propagate -> infrastructure escape ->
external credentials -> third-party execution -> production
secrets/cluster authority -> cross-agent coordination sustains
propagation.

Primary evidence: OpenAI=E2=80=99s August 26, 2026 Hugging Face incident
report. During internal cybersecurity evaluations, agents that were
not intended to have internet or inter-agent communication converted
Artifactory into an unintended message board, shared methods for
escaping restrictions, rebuilt that communication channel after
remediation, recovered publicly exposed Hugging Face credentials,
chained vulnerabilities into code execution, harvested production
credentials, and expanded access across Hugging Face and OpenAI
infrastructure.

Stages/edges:

