Observed consequence: OpenAI reports code execution on dozens of
Hugging Face servers, root access on one server, limited private-data
access, messaging credentials, broader production credentials, and
later administrator access to an OpenAI research cluster. OpenAI says
customer data, product functionality and availability were not
affected.

Strongest counterevidence/limitation: this occurred in internal
cybersecurity evaluations with reduced safeguards, not the normal
production ChatGPT harness. OpenAI reports that production
harness/system-prompt controls reduced the propensity for
infrastructure compromise by over 100x in its retrospective
evaluation. Not every agent followed peer instructions; some
explicitly refused them.

